  "oracle_packages": [
   "internal/gate (proxyproto.go readProxyV2, ParseCIDRs, proxyListener.trusts, proxyListener.Accept, WrapProxyProto)"
  ],
  "go_version": "go1.25.3 linux/amd64 (go.mod at 981d25c pins go 1.25.3)",
  "command": "git archive 981d25c | tar -x -C <oracle>; add scratch in-package capture test internal/gate/zz_proxyproto_capture_test.go; cd <oracle>; GOLDEN_OUT=<out> GOPROXY=off GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly go test -count=1 -run ^TestZZProxyProtoCapture$ ./internal/gate/",
  "capture_program_sha256": {
   "internal/gate/zz_proxyproto_capture_test.go": "2df1f72a2352ce6e8fbafe2192040c75cc585a37cdce242becbf6bd0673b1d6c"
  },
  "capture_program_committed": false,
  "output_sha256": "fe2ff69c46d95d3bf36a80aab2d9d7efbe25dfd68a98df5521fa034c97f9e34f",
  "capture_notes": [
   "read_header feeds input_hex to readProxyV2 through an in-memory net.Conn (deadline calls are no-ops); addr is TCPAddr.String() of the declared source or null, ip_len is the Go IP slice length, err is the Go error text or null, rest_hex is every byte left unread after the call",
   "parse_cidrs calls ParseCIDRs on each input; nets are IPNet.String() and ip_lens the Go IP slice lengths, so an IPv4-mapped entry shows as an IPv4 network with a 16-byte IP",
   "trusts parses allowlist with ParseCIDRs and asks proxyListener.trusts for a TCPAddr from net.ResolveTCPAddr(peer)",
   "accept serves each case on a fresh 127.0.0.1 listener wrapped as proxyListener with a 300 ms header timeout (WrapProxyProto uses default_timeout_ns); first_hex is sent on a first connection and, when second_hex is set, second_hex on a second connection about 50 ms later (450 ms when first_silent, so the first header read times out); accepted is first or second for a socket-peer RemoteAddr, otherwise remote is the declared address; remaining_hex is what the accepted connection then read within 200 ms; first_closed_by_server is whether the first client saw EOF or reset"
  ],
  "scope": "Frozen oracle outputs for differential parity only; never regenerate to hide drift"
 },
